# AGENTS.md

pandocea turns markdown into Google Docs. Its first product is `piers`, an MCP
moxin (Google Docs: read, create, edit, comment, rename) that moxy serves; the
converter is a pandoc custom Lua writer plus a request runtime.

## Layout

- `moxins/piers/` -- the moxin: one TOML per tool and `src/*.ts` (bun + zx).
  `src/docs-requests.lua` is the pandoc writer that emits Docs API
  `batchUpdate` requests; `src/docs-markdown.ts` sends them; `src/images.ts`
  renders and hosts images and PlantUML diagrams; `src/gws.ts` is piers' layer
  over the gws runner.
- `moxin-lib/gws-run.ts` -- the gws runner: gws runs from a scratch directory
  and a failure is one line. Copied from moxy, where car, prison, gmail and
  calendar share it; keep the two in step until a common home exists.
- `zz-tests_bats/piers_*.bats`, `piers_stub.bash` -- bats against a stub gws.
  They still `load 'common'` from moxy's helper library, so they do not run
  here until it is ported.
- `zz-pocs/pandoc-docs-poc/` -- the experiment the writer grew from.

## Build

- `just build` builds `.#piers` with a standalone read-policy stand-in.
- Consumers (moxy) call `pandocea.lib.<system>.mkPiers folioPerms`, passing
  their own read-policy script for the `@FOLIO_PERMS@` placeholder in the
  create and update tomls.
- `GWS_BIN` names the gws binary; tests point it at a stub.

## Conventions

- Justfile recipes are the paved paths; do not run ad hoc shell for repeated
  work.
- `version.env` is the one version source.
- Moxin dependencies come through nix wrapping (`mkBunMoxin`), never ambient
  PATH.
